              "start": 104,
              "end": 220,
              "quote": "从诗歌和歌曲中摘录句子并以这种方式加以运用，是一个令人自豪的传统。有些人认为，小说和戏剧里的句子离不开它们的上下文。东摘一句、西摘一句是不恰当的。我不同意这种看法。它忽视了大脑收集、整理和组合信息的方式。我们能从一切事物中找到意义。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "translation-paragraph:group:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:seven-choices:3",
              "sourceParagraphIds": [
                "block:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:seven-choices:3"
              ],
              "start": 222,
              "end": 347,
              "quote": "如今，我们常常把日程排得过满，还不停抱怨太忙。书籍特别适合帮助我们改变自己与日常生活节奏和习惯之间的关系。它们需要我们投入注意力。它们要求我们暂时放下手头的工作，去倾听别人的声音。你可以对着一本书咆哮，甚至把它扔出窗外。但你仍然改变不了书页上的文字。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "translation-paragraph:group:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:seven-choices:4",
              "sourceParagraphIds": [
                "block:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:seven-choices:4"
              ],
              "start": 349,
              "end": 455,
              "quote": "我们彼此会问很多问题：“你睡得怎么样？”“你假期去哪儿了？”但有一个问题我们应该更常问问彼此，那就是：“你在读什么？”如果带着真诚的好奇心去问，这就不是一个简单的问题。它其实是了解你正在成为什么样的人的一种方式。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "translation-paragraph:group:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:seven-choices:5",
              "sourceParagraphIds": [
                "block:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:seven-choices:5"
              ],
              "start": 457,
              "end": 578,
              "quote": "你还可以通过评估作者的写作技巧，如思想、措辞、风格、语气和内容，来了解写这本书的人。对这些方面加以分析，能揭示出作者的一些情况。同样，审视书中的人物能让我们更好地理解人类的情感和行为。理解他人有助于我们与之共情，从而创造一个更富同情心的社会。"
            }
          ]
        },
        "completedSourceTexts": [
          {
            "textId": "completed:blank:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:36",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:seven-choices:1",
            "text": "It’s believed that everything you need to know can be found in a book. People have always received life-guiding wisdom from certain types of non-fiction, often from “self-help” books. But actually all sorts of books can carry this kind of wisdom. A random sentence in a thriller(惊悚小说) will give you unexpected insight."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:blank:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:37",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:seven-choices:2",
            "text": "There is a proud tradition of extracting(摘录) lines from poetry and songs and using them in this way. Some people argue that lines from novels and plays are dependent on what surrounds them. It’s improper to grab the odd line here and there. I don’t buy this. It ignores the way that your brain collects, sorts and combines information. We can find meaning in everything."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:blank:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:38",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:seven-choices:3",
            "text": "Today, we often over-schedule our days and complain constantly about being too busy. Books are uniquely suited to helping us change our relationship to the rhythms and habits of daily life. They demand our attention. They demand that we briefly put aside our work at hand and listen to someone else. You can rant against(咆哮)a book, or even throw it out the window. Still, you won’t change the words on the page."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:blank:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:39",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:seven-choices:4",
            "text": "We all ask each other a lot of questions: “How did you sleep?” “Where did you go on your holidays?” But there’s one question we should ask of one another a lot more often, and that is: “What are you reading?” It isn’t a simple question when asked with genuine curiosity. It’s really a way of finding out what you are becoming."
          },
          {
            "textId": "completed:blank:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:40",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-zhejiang-jiangzhewan-2024-10:seven-choices:5",
            "text": "You can also learn about the person who wrote the book by assessing their writing techniques, such as ideas, word choice, style, tone, and content. An analysis of these aspects can reveal things about the author. Similarly, examining the characters in books can give us a better grasp of human emotions and actions. Understanding others helps us to empathize with them, which creates a more compassionate society."
          }
        ],
